  "details": "With the increasing capabilities of color passthrough with accurate depth projection in various devices, exciting opportunities arise for blending the real and virtual worlds within VRChat. Currently, PC users leverage chroma key worlds and avatar addons in conjunction with Virtual Desktop to create mixed reality environments with avatars. However, this method presents limitations. It would be highly advantageous to introduce a dedicated passthrough mode for standalone users, where avatar and UI render layers seamlessly overlay the HMD's passthrough image. While Virtual Desktop remains the sole option for PC users at present, offering built-in chroma key tools within the native passthrough layer would enhance flexibility and accessibility. Ultimately, this proposal aims to bridge the gap between VRChat's vibrant social scene and the physical world, fostering a deeper sense of room presence without the constraints of PC dependence, specific worlds, or specific avatars.",
